  You have a good point.  The chance of distorting an engraving while
moving off of it is another reason to do several dust Elbereths with an
item on.


  Engraving one "Elbereth" at a time exercises wisdom and seems to
minimize the chance of obscuring any earlier engravings.  NB: obscuring
is not the same as rubbing out.  Obscuring is apparently temporary and
only lasts for as long as you're engraving.

  Note also that there's a limit on how many letters you can have
engraved on a single square.  After a certain point you're just
increasing the chance of rubbing out previous engravings without adding
new engravings.  So just madly pasting "E- Elbereth" will eventually get
you killed.  (Took too many lessons to teach me that.)

  Even once you have a few avoidance squares peaceful and tame monsters
can and will mess them up.  They can even ruin them by just taking the
item while not disturbing the engraving.

  This gives a new use for darts/glass/gems.  Being light items they're
useful for such squares.



